  "meta-description": "Build a law firm landing page for each practice area, with intake questions, a conflict check and every inquiry routed to the right attorney.",
  "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>Copy and fee changes by message</h3><p>Ask Emergent to raise the consult fee, add a Spanish version or swap the headshot. The page updates at the same address, and inquiries saved before the change stay in the table.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Law Firm Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a law firm landing page?\", \"a\": \"A law firm landing page is a single page built for one practice area and one goal, like a free case review for car crash victims. It has no site menu, and its form feeds the firm's intake. Ads and local search results point to it instead of the home page.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you design a landing page for lawyers?\", \"a\": \"Start with one case type, then put that case type, the attorney's name, and a short form on the first screen of a phone. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe that page in a prompt, and Emergent builds it along with the intake rules behind the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the best law firm landing pages have in common?\", \"a\": \"The best law firm landing pages stick to one case type and one ask. They show the attorney who handles the matter and explain fees plainly. Like any lead generation landing page, the form asks only what the first call needs.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a law firm landing page template?\", \"a\": \"Unbounce keeps a gallery of legal landing page templates. A template gives you the layout of a lawyer landing page but stops at the form. Emergent writes the page and its intake from one prompt instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are there free lawyer landing page templates?\", \"a\": \"Figma's community has free law firm files, though a design file is a picture of a page rather than a working one. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing landing pages for lawyers with a working form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an attorney landing page include?\", \"a\": \"An attorney landing page needs a headline that names the case type and a form with few fields. Add proof a visitor can check, such as the attorney's bar admissions and years in practice. Send each submission to a thank you page that says when the firm will call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do PPC landing pages for law firms differ from the firm's website?\", \"a\": \"A website serves every visitor, while PPC landing pages for law firms serve one ad group, such as DUI arrests in one county. Each page repeats the ad's wording and drops the menu. The same habits apply to any ppc landing page: one keyword theme and one form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes a good lawyer landing page example?\", \"a\": \"A good example targets one problem in one county, like a bankruptcy firm's page for people facing wage garnishment. The headline names the problem, the form asks for the county and whether a court date is set, and the page books a call with the attorney who covers that county.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a law firm hire a web design agency for landing pages?\", \"a\": \"An agency suits a full firm website with custom photography and a long build. Lawyer landing pages change with every campaign and practice area, which favors a tool the firm edits itself. On Emergent, a message such as 'aim the headline at truck accidents' rewrites the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find inspiration for lawyer landing page design?\", \"a\": \"Dribbble collects law firm landing page concepts from designers. Study them for layout and type. Then look at what each page does once the form is sent, which galleries rarely show.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "alpb---how-to-step-5-des": "A phone number, the type of case and one qualifying answer cover most first calls. Leave the full story for the consultation, where an attorney can ask follow-up questions and explain what the firm does with the answers."
 }
}